WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.115 --> 00:00:02.075
STATIONED IN JAPAN.

00:00:02.076 --> 00:00:02.460
MOLLY.

00:00:02.493 --> 00:00:03.967
MOLLY:  ALARMING NEW RESEARCH

00:00:04.001 --> 00:00:05.860
MAY TELL US WHY HOUSTON IS

00:00:05.894 --> 00:00:08.221
SEEING SUCH A HIGH SPIKE IN

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:10.481
CORONAVIRUS CASES WITH HOUSTON’S

00:00:10.483 --> 00:00:12.904
TEXAS MEDICAL CENTER REPORTEDLY

00:00:12.906 --> 00:00:14.656
AT 105% CAPACITY.

00:00:14.657 --> 00:00:16.486
RESEARCHERS AT BAYLOR COLLEGE OF

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.375
MEDICINE SAY A STRAIN OF THE

00:00:18.409 --> 00:00:20.690
VIRUS IN THE AREA HAS MUTATED

00:00:20.724 --> 00:00:21.967
AND HAS BECOME EVEN MORE

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:23.164
CONTAGIOUS THAN WHAT WE HAVE

00:00:23.165 --> 00:00:25.529
SEEN SO FAR.

00:00:25.530 --> 00:00:28.654
JOINING ME NOW, DR. CEDRIC DARK,

00:00:28.656 --> 00:00:30.305
EMERGENCY MEDICINE PHYSICIAN AND

00:00:30.307 --> 00:00:31.984
ASSISTANT PROFESSOR AT BAYLOR

00:00:31.985 --> 00:00:34.129
COLLEGE OF MEDICINE, THE FOUNDER

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.867
OF POLICY PRESCRIPTION AND A

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:36.927
BOARD MEMBER OF DOCTORS FOR

00:00:36.962 --> 00:00:37.345
AMERICA.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.676
THANK YOU FOR BEING HERE WITH US

00:00:39.677 --> 00:00:40.209
TODAY.

00:00:40.210 --> 00:00:42.420
WE HAVE BEEN FOLLOWING A NUMBER

00:00:42.421 --> 00:00:44.608
OF STATES THAT HAVE SEEN A SPIKE

00:00:44.609 --> 00:00:46.338
IN CASES ALONG THE SUN BELT.

00:00:46.339 --> 00:00:47.738
IF YOU COULD GIVE US INSIDE TO

00:00:47.773 --> 00:00:48.894
START THE CONVERSATION ABOUT

00:00:48.928 --> 00:00:50.149
WHAT YOU’RE SEEING IN TEXAS,

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:51.546
MORE SPECIFICALLY IN HOUSTON.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.552
&gt;&gt;  YESTERDAY WAS TEXAS’

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:54.912
DEADLIEST DAY OF THE PANDEMIC,

00:00:54.913 --> 00:00:56.704
OVER 100 PEOPLE DIED.

00:00:56.739 --> 00:00:58.324
AND I’VE SEEN REPORTS THAT

00:00:58.325 --> 00:00:59.608
REFRIGERATED TRUCKS ARE COMING

00:00:59.642 --> 00:01:01.515
INTO TEXAS TO BE ABLE TO HANDLE

00:01:01.549 --> 00:01:02.803
BODIES BECAUSE THERE ARE NOT

00:01:02.804 --> 00:01:03.955
ENOUGH SPACES IN THE MORGUES.

00:01:03.956 --> 00:01:05.229
THIS IS SOMETHING THAT I

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.108
EXPERIENCED ONE OTHER TIME, BACK

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:08.510
WHEN I WAS IN MEDICAL SCHOOL,

00:01:08.544 --> 00:01:09.489
2001, DURING 9/11.

00:01:09.523 --> 00:01:11.905
I ACTUALLY WENT TO MEDICAL

00:01:11.907 --> 00:01:13.974
SCHOOL IN NEW YORK AND FROM MY

00:01:14.009 --> 00:01:15.731
14th FLOOR I COULD SEE ONTO

00:01:15.766 --> 00:01:17.711
THE OFFICE OF THE CHIEF MEDICAL

00:01:17.712 --> 00:01:20.091
EXAMINER AND I COULD SEE ROWS OF

00:01:20.126 --> 00:01:21.420
REFRIGERATED TRUCKS, A WHITE

00:01:21.454 --> 00:01:22.918
TARP THAT CARRIED THE BODIES OF

00:01:22.919 --> 00:01:24.819
THE PEOPLE THAT WERE KILLED IN

00:01:24.853 --> 00:01:26.398
THE COLLAPSE OF THE TWIN TOWERS.

00:01:26.399 --> 00:01:27.666
BUT JUST TO PUT IT IN

00:01:27.667 --> 00:01:28.670
PERSPECTIVE, MORE PEOPLE HAVE

00:01:28.704 --> 00:01:31.563
DIED IN TEXAS FROM COVID THAN

00:01:31.564 --> 00:01:33.250
THOSE WHO DIED DURING THE 9/11

00:01:33.285 --> 00:01:33.899
ATTACKS.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.453
MOLLY:  IT’S SOMETHING

00:01:35.487 --> 00:01:36.648
PARTICULARLY SCARY BECAUSE WE’RE

00:01:36.649 --> 00:01:38.092
HARDLY CLOSE TO THE END OF THIS

00:01:38.093 --> 00:01:38.896
AT ALL.

00:01:38.897 --> 00:01:41.701
AND NOW WE’RE SEEING THIS NEW

00:01:41.702 --> 00:01:43.832
RESEARCH, SO THIS IS THE

00:01:43.834 --> 00:01:44.963
NATIONAL LABORATORY, THEY

00:01:44.965 --> 00:01:47.129
DISCOVERED A MUTATION OF THE

00:01:47.163 --> 00:01:48.445
VIRUS THAT FACILITATES ITS

00:01:48.446 --> 00:01:49.369
SPREAD.

00:01:49.403 --> 00:01:52.543
JOSEPH PETROZINO WHO IS THE

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.451
CHAIR OF MICROBIOLOGY AT BAYLOR

00:01:54.486 --> 00:01:56.072
COLLEGE OF MEDICINE, HE SAYS THE

00:01:56.073 --> 00:01:58.588
ONE WE HAVE IN THE U.S. SPREADS

00:01:58.623 --> 00:02:00.255
BETTER THAN THE ORIGINALLY, THAT

00:02:00.289 --> 00:02:02.008
ORIGINALLY EMERGED IN CHINA.

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.996
WHAT DOES THIS MEAN FOR HOUSTON,

00:02:04.030 --> 00:02:05.739
FOR THE HOUSTON AREA,

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:07.227
POTENTIALLY FOR THE COUNTRY?

00:02:07.228 --> 00:02:10.287
&gt;&gt; IT MEANS IT’S EASIER FOR THE

00:02:10.289 --> 00:02:12.347
DISEASE TO SPREAD AND FOR MORE

00:02:12.348 --> 00:02:13.673
PEOPLE TO GET INFECTED.

00:02:13.674 --> 00:02:14.727
PEOPLE NEED TO TAKE THIS

00:02:14.761 --> 00:02:14.954
SERIOUSLY.

00:02:14.955 --> 00:02:16.331
WE NEED TO MAKE SURE THAT

00:02:16.365 --> 00:02:17.632
EVERYBODY IS MASKING UP WHEN

00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:18.744
THEY’RE OUT IN PUBLIC.

00:02:18.746 --> 00:02:19.918
PEOPLE NEED TO SOCIALLY DISTANCE

00:02:19.952 --> 00:02:20.863
FROM PEOPLE THAT AREN’T IN THEIR

00:02:20.864 --> 00:02:21.333
HOMES.

00:02:21.367 --> 00:02:23.346
IF WE DON’T, WE’RE GOING TO LOSE

00:02:23.347 --> 00:02:24.433
CONTROL OF THE VIRUS.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:25.772
YOU SEE WHAT’S ALREADY HAPPENED

00:02:25.807 --> 00:02:26.787
IN TEXAS.

00:02:26.822 --> 00:02:29.680
WE HAD A PRETTY GOOD GRIP ON IT

00:02:29.681 --> 00:02:32.396
EARLIER ON IN THE PANDEMIC IN

00:02:32.397 --> 00:02:34.892
APRIL AND GOING INTO MAY, UNTIL

00:02:34.927 --> 00:02:36.520
WE REOPENED OUR ECONOMY AT A

00:02:36.554 --> 00:02:37.502
BREAKNECK PACE.

00:02:37.504 --> 00:02:40.023
ONCE WE DID THAT, CASES STARTED

00:02:40.057 --> 00:02:41.243
GOING UP DRAMATICALLY,

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:43.683
INCREASING OVER THE PAST TWO TO

00:02:43.717 --> 00:02:45.147
THREE WEEKS ALMOST AT AN

00:02:45.148 --> 00:02:45.845
EXPONENTIAL RATE.

00:02:45.846 --> 00:02:48.373
NOW WE’RE TRYING TO GET A HANDLE

00:02:48.374 --> 00:02:50.449
ON IT AGAIN, TO THE POINT WHERE

00:02:50.451 --> 00:02:51.813
THE GOVERNOR HAD TO REISSUE A

00:02:51.814 --> 00:02:52.926
MASK ORDER.

00:02:52.928 --> 00:02:55.759
THERE WAS A PERIOD OF 67 DAYS

00:02:55.793 --> 00:02:57.598
WHERE THE GOVERNOR PROHIBITED

00:02:57.632 --> 00:03:01.018
PEOPLE IN HOUSTON FROM ISSUING

00:03:01.019 --> 00:03:04.093
OR ISSUINGOUR OWN MASK ORDER UNT

00:03:04.094 --> 00:03:06.141
FORCED TO DO IT FOR THE ENTIRE

00:03:06.142 --> 00:03:06.653
STATE.

00:03:06.654 --> 00:03:09.056
MOLLY:  YOUR THOUGHTS ON THE

00:03:09.058 --> 00:03:11.202
SUGGESTION THERE SHOULD BE A

00:03:11.203 --> 00:03:12.407
NATIONWIDE MASK MANDATE, AS

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:14.447
OPPOSED TO STATE BY STATE.

00:03:14.481 --> 00:03:16.299
&gt;&gt;  I THINK HEALTHCARE IS BEST

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:16.780
DELIVERED LOCALLY.

00:03:16.814 --> 00:03:19.216
WHAT WE SHOULD BE DOING IS

00:03:19.251 --> 00:03:22.102
TRYING TO HAVE DECISIONS MADE BY

00:03:22.137 --> 00:03:23.463
LOCAL POLITICIANS AT ALL COSTS,

00:03:23.498 --> 00:03:24.435
IF WE CAN.

00:03:24.436 --> 00:03:26.618
I THINK IT’S A MISTAKE FOR

00:03:26.619 --> 00:03:28.778
SOMEONE TO COME IN AND OVERRULE

00:03:28.779 --> 00:03:30.779
WHAT THE LOCAL POLITICIANS WANT

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.944
TO DO IF THAT MEANS THEY WANT TO

00:03:34.978 --> 00:03:37.261
MASK AND IF IT BECOMES NECESSARY

00:03:37.262 --> 00:03:39.390
AS IT BECAME NECESSARY IN TEXAS

00:03:39.425 --> 00:03:40.976
FOR THE SAKE OF PUBLIC HEALTH,

00:03:40.977 --> 00:03:42.381
WE NEED A MASK ORDER.

00:03:42.383 --> 00:03:43.448
WHETHER OR NOT WE NEED ONE

00:03:43.449 --> 00:03:45.004
NATIONALLY, I THINK AT THIS

00:03:45.006 --> 00:03:46.396
POINT IT SHOULD BE A STATE BY

00:03:46.397 --> 00:03:47.255
STATE DECISION.

00:03:47.257 --> 00:03:48.678
IF IT’S OVERWHELMING THE ENTIRE

00:03:48.679 --> 00:03:50.425
COUNTRY, I WOULD CALL ON THE

00:03:50.427 --> 00:03:51.509
PRESIDENT TO MAKE THAT ORDER AS

00:03:51.511 --> 00:03:52.393
WELL.

00:03:52.394 --> 00:03:55.613
MOLLY:  HOUSTON AMONG OTHER

00:03:55.647 --> 00:03:57.564
CITIES IN THE SOUTH, AND

00:03:57.565 --> 00:03:59.105
ARIZONA, SOME IN FLORIDA HAVE

00:03:59.139 --> 00:04:00.716
BEEN DESCRIBED AS HOT SPOTS.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:02.657
HOW DO YOU CLIMB OUT OF THAT?

00:04:02.691 --> 00:04:04.023
WHAT IS THE STRATEGY?

00:04:04.057 --> 00:04:05.995
WHAT DO PEOPLE NEED TO DO?

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.291
WHAT DO PROVIDERS NEED TO DO,

00:04:07.292 --> 00:04:08.664
ALSO THE GOVERNMENT THAT ARE

00:04:08.665 --> 00:04:09.570
SPEAKING AND WORKING TO INFORM

00:04:09.571 --> 00:04:10.146
THE PEOPLE.

00:04:10.147 --> 00:04:11.469
&gt;&gt;  I THINK WE NEED CONSISTENT

00:04:11.503 --> 00:04:12.981
LEADERSHIP FROM THE TOP DOWN.

00:04:13.016 --> 00:04:15.447
AS I SAID BEFORE, I’LL REITERATE

00:04:15.449 --> 00:04:16.855
NOW, MASKING, SOCIAL DISTANCING

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:17.769
AND TAKING THE CORONAVIRUS

00:04:17.803 --> 00:04:18.660
SERIOUSLY IS WHAT WE DEFINITELY

00:04:18.694 --> 00:04:19.310
NEED TO DO.

00:04:19.311 --> 00:04:21.494
ONE OF THE OTHER THINGS THAT WE

00:04:21.496 --> 00:04:23.027
HAVE TO REALIZE IS THAT OUR

00:04:23.028 --> 00:04:24.665
TREATMENTS IN THE MEDICAL FIELD

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:26.206
ARE FAIRLY LIMITED.

00:04:26.240 --> 00:04:30.137
WE HAVE OXYGEN THAT WE CAN GIVE

00:04:30.139 --> 00:04:31.039
TO PATIENTS, ANTI-VIRAL

00:04:31.073 --> 00:04:33.867
REMDESIVIR THAT WE CAN GIVE TO

00:04:33.902 --> 00:04:37.968
PEOPLE TO SHORTEN HOSPITAL

00:04:38.002 --> 00:04:38.721
STAYS.

00:04:38.723 --> 00:04:41.419
WHEN IT COMES TO THE SIMPLE

00:04:41.453 --> 00:04:42.595
INTERVENTIONS, SOMETHING AS EASY

00:04:42.596 --> 00:04:43.656
AS OXYGEN, HAVE YOU TO THINK

00:04:43.657 --> 00:04:45.231
ABOUT HOW MUCH DOES THAT COST

00:04:45.233 --> 00:04:46.659
FOR SOMEONE TO ACTUALLY TAKE

00:04:46.693 --> 00:04:49.215
CARE OF THAT AT HOME.

00:04:49.249 --> 00:04:51.798
I WAS LOOKING UP, HOW MUCH IS AN

00:04:51.799 --> 00:04:53.547
OXYGEN CONCENTRATOR, IT’S ON THE

00:04:53.548 --> 00:04:55.285
ORDER OF HUNDREDS TO UP TO

00:04:55.286 --> 00:04:56.840
$3,000 FOR THAT MACHINE.

00:04:56.841 --> 00:04:59.394
WHAT DO YOU DO IN TEXAS WHERE

00:04:59.428 --> 00:05:00.756
YOU HAVE 18% OF THE POPULATION

00:05:00.791 --> 00:05:00.989
UNINSURED.

00:05:01.023 --> 00:05:02.984
HOW ARE WE GOING TO MAKE SURE

00:05:03.019 --> 00:05:04.695
THAT PEOPLE THAT NEED SUCH A

00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:05.586
SIMPLE THERAPY HAVE ACCESS TO

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:05.890
IT.

00:05:05.925 --> 00:05:08.160
SO WHAT I WOULD SAY RIGHT NOW IS

00:05:08.161 --> 00:05:09.703
WE HAVE A MORAL IMPERATIVE TO

00:05:09.737 --> 00:05:11.722
ONE ANOTHER TO ADDRESS THINGS

00:05:11.723 --> 00:05:14.788
LIKE THE SOCIAL DETERMINANTS OF

00:05:14.822 --> 00:05:16.242
HEALTH, THINGS LIKE

00:05:16.276 --> 00:05:18.126
UNININSURANCE SO PEOPLE THAT ARE

00:05:18.127 --> 00:05:20.224
SICK CAN GET THE CARE THEY NEED

00:05:20.226 --> 00:05:23.167
SO THEY CAN RECOVER AND RETURN

00:05:23.168 --> 00:05:24.585
TO BEING FUNCTIONAL MEMBERS OF

00:05:24.587 --> 00:05:25.259
SOCIETY.

